1
00:01:54,511 --> 00:01:56,511
Hey. Don't we have any more booze?

2
00:01:56,591 --> 00:01:57,721
It's my painkiller.

3
00:02:00,181 --> 00:02:01,141
Damn.

4
00:02:01,221 --> 00:02:03,181
Aren't we there yet?

5
00:02:03,261 --> 00:02:05,601
That place where they're supposed
to give us the money.

6
00:02:06,181 --> 00:02:09,141
Don't be in such a hurry.
We're almost there.

7
00:02:11,731 --> 00:02:14,361
The Troll's Son

8
00:02:34,921 --> 00:02:35,921
Damn.

9
00:02:39,051 --> 00:02:40,431
Damn it.

10
00:02:51,901 --> 00:02:54,401
-My whole body hurts.
-I want to find me a nice girl.

11
00:02:54,481 --> 00:02:55,861
ENGLAND
VICINITY OF HUMBER RIVER

12
00:02:56,691 --> 00:02:58,531
Who's going to watch the ships?

13
00:02:58,611 --> 00:03:00,611
We're just here to rest our bones.

14
00:03:00,701 --> 00:03:02,661
We're not going to stay here for long.

15
00:04:42,761 --> 00:04:44,221
Get up.

16
00:04:44,301 --> 00:04:46,341
Hey. Don't run away.
I'll kill you if you move.

17
00:04:46,931 --> 00:04:50,431
Don't let anyone get away.
We're going to have trouble if this gets out.

18
00:04:52,891 --> 00:04:54,351
Two on the right.

19
00:05:47,451 --> 00:05:51,451
And then the guy ate it.
He didn't even know what it was.

20
00:07:09,951 --> 00:07:12,361
-My head hurts.
-I drank too much.

21
00:07:16,331 --> 00:07:18,621
What happened?
Did you have a hard time falling asleep?

22
00:07:20,211 --> 00:07:22,001
There was a noisy little fly in my room.

23
00:07:22,081 --> 00:07:23,131
A little fly?

24
00:07:27,711 --> 00:07:29,631
Who's that? A survivor?

25
00:07:30,131 --> 00:07:33,761
No. It's the son. The Troll of Jom's kid.

26
00:07:33,841 --> 00:07:36,011
He's still alive?

27
00:07:36,101 --> 00:07:38,431
Too much trouble for the early morning.

28
00:07:39,641 --> 00:07:41,481
This is revenge for my father.

29
00:07:41,561 --> 00:07:43,271
I challenge you to a duel.

30
00:07:44,351 --> 00:07:46,061
Impressive, kid.

31
00:07:46,151 --> 00:07:47,901
I'm so scared.

32
00:07:49,781 --> 00:07:52,031
What are you going to do, Askeladd?

33
00:07:53,861 --> 00:07:55,411
What a pain.

34
00:07:56,451 --> 00:07:57,781
Come on.

35
00:07:57,871 --> 00:08:00,501
You should have cut off my head
while I was asleep.

36
00:08:03,251 --> 00:08:05,041
I'm the son of Thors.

37
00:08:10,011 --> 00:08:12,051
I'd never do something

38
00:08:12,131 --> 00:08:13,511
so cowardly.

39
00:08:15,891 --> 00:08:17,011
Wow, I'm so scared.

40
00:08:17,101 --> 00:08:21,021
-Did you hear that, Askeladd?
-Kill him, kid.

41
00:08:21,101 --> 00:08:22,141
Get him.

42
00:08:22,231 --> 00:08:24,561
So, you think you're a warrior?

43
00:08:25,601 --> 00:08:27,191
All right. Come at me.

44
00:08:42,451 --> 00:08:43,871
Yeah. Just like that.

45
00:08:46,711 --> 00:08:49,381
Someone dig him a grave.

46
00:08:49,461 --> 00:08:51,131
Damn. Damn.

47
00:08:51,881 --> 00:08:55,341
You can't let your sword
swing you around like that.

48
00:09:01,061 --> 00:09:02,681
You're so brutal.

49
00:09:02,771 --> 00:09:04,731
Maybe he's dead already.

50
00:09:06,351 --> 00:09:07,941
Come on.

51
00:09:20,081 --> 00:09:22,581
We confirmed it.

52
00:09:22,661 --> 00:09:24,001
Here's your money.

53
00:09:27,671 --> 00:09:29,751
Thank you very much.

54
00:09:30,791 --> 00:09:33,761
Say thanks to Floki for me.

55
00:09:39,181 --> 00:09:42,311
I can't get too friendly with the villagers.

56
00:09:45,181 --> 00:09:47,441
By the way, I have a message for you.

57
00:09:48,401 --> 00:09:49,311
A message?

58
00:09:49,901 --> 00:09:53,571
"How was Thors's final moment?"

59
00:09:58,951 --> 00:09:59,991
It was nothing special.

60
00:10:01,331 --> 00:10:04,371
He just died a normal death.

61
00:10:14,211 --> 00:10:15,841
What? You're still alive?

62
00:10:16,421 --> 00:10:18,341
You look terrible.

63
00:10:18,431 --> 00:10:19,551
Want some?

64
00:10:25,141 --> 00:10:27,351
It's not healthy to deprive yourself.

65
00:10:34,151 --> 00:10:35,481
What's wrong with him?

66
00:10:35,571 --> 00:10:37,241
We were only trying to help.

67
00:10:45,371 --> 00:10:46,371
Damn.

68
00:11:24,871 --> 00:11:26,161
Damn it.

69
00:11:29,081 --> 00:11:31,961
Damn it all.

70
00:11:39,421 --> 00:11:42,051
He died an honorable death.

71
00:11:42,761 --> 00:11:45,431
Thors sacrificed himself for us.

72
00:11:48,521 --> 00:11:51,731
I'm sorry, Helga. Ylva.

73
00:11:51,811 --> 00:11:55,311
My words cannot express how sorry I am.

74
00:12:01,741 --> 00:12:04,571
He's already dead.
No one can do anything about it now.

75
00:12:04,661 --> 00:12:06,781
Crying about it will just make you hungry.

76
00:12:11,121 --> 00:12:13,171
Time to get back to work.

77
00:12:17,421 --> 00:12:18,421
Helga.

78
00:12:20,131 --> 00:12:21,631
Thorfinn...

79
00:12:21,721 --> 00:12:24,761
I'm going to find him, no matter what.

80
00:12:26,341 --> 00:12:28,351
No matter how many years it takes.

81
00:12:32,431 --> 00:12:36,771
Well, I never thought he'd live a long life anyway.

82
00:12:37,311 --> 00:12:40,901
It's hard having a strange dad like him.

83
00:12:40,981 --> 00:12:43,901
Your little brother is missing, too, right?

84
00:12:43,991 --> 00:12:45,861
Are you okay, Ylva?

85
00:12:45,951 --> 00:12:48,911
I'm so busy, now that the men are all gone.

86
00:12:50,541 --> 00:12:51,621
Ylva.

87
00:12:53,501 --> 00:12:55,041
Yeah.

88
00:12:55,121 --> 00:12:56,581
You're crazy, Ylva.

89
00:13:00,381 --> 00:13:01,961
Mother, how are you feeling?

90
00:13:02,551 --> 00:13:05,221
Yes. I feel much better.

91
00:13:05,301 --> 00:13:07,181
Sorry to rely so much on you, Ylva--

92
00:13:07,261 --> 00:13:08,091
Okay, okay.

93
00:13:08,801 --> 00:13:10,761
It's okay. Don't get up.

94
00:13:15,981 --> 00:13:17,811
Oops, I forgot about the sheep.

95
00:13:21,071 --> 00:13:23,861
Okay, okay. Sorry I'm late.

96
00:13:28,821 --> 00:13:32,241
I must shear the sheep when spring comes too.

97
00:13:39,541 --> 00:13:42,091
Yeah.

98
00:13:43,341 --> 00:13:45,841
I got the first hit.

99
00:13:50,141 --> 00:13:52,011
I'm so busy.

100
00:13:52,721 --> 00:13:55,601
We don't have enough people to pitch in.

101
00:13:55,681 --> 00:13:57,391
Maybe I should get a husband.

102
00:14:01,361 --> 00:14:02,571
Thanks.

103
00:14:03,611 --> 00:14:04,861
Let's go to sleep.

104
00:14:06,991 --> 00:14:08,951
You can go to sleep first.

105
00:14:09,031 --> 00:14:10,821
I'm going to finish this.

106
00:14:12,951 --> 00:14:16,001
But it's dark already.

107
00:14:16,081 --> 00:14:17,831
You'll make a mistake.

108
00:14:20,501 --> 00:14:21,331
Ylva.

109
00:14:27,051 --> 00:14:28,971
That's enough.

110
00:14:29,051 --> 00:14:30,141
Get some rest.

111
00:14:30,221 --> 00:14:32,761
But I'm almost done.

112
00:14:32,851 --> 00:14:35,851
I'm okay. I'm not tired.

113
00:15:10,051 --> 00:15:11,381
I'm going to kill him.

114
00:15:12,511 --> 00:15:15,261
I'm going to kill him, no matter what.

115
00:15:24,981 --> 00:15:25,821
Hey.

116
00:15:27,191 --> 00:15:28,491
You're working hard.

117
00:15:29,571 --> 00:15:30,571
You.

118
00:15:31,111 --> 00:15:32,451
How is it?

119
00:15:32,531 --> 00:15:34,491
Have you gotten used to using a sword?

120
00:15:38,161 --> 00:15:40,461
You. It's your fault.

121
00:15:40,541 --> 00:15:42,291
You used me as a shield.

122
00:15:43,331 --> 00:15:44,461
That's why my father...

123
00:15:46,461 --> 00:15:48,211
You coward.

124
00:15:49,551 --> 00:15:52,591
Your father really was strong.

125
00:15:52,681 --> 00:15:54,391
But he was naive.

126
00:15:54,471 --> 00:15:55,721
That's all there is to it.

127
00:15:56,301 --> 00:15:59,601
Don't make fun of my father!

128
00:16:09,361 --> 00:16:12,951
Well. You're just weak.

129
00:16:26,671 --> 00:16:27,791
Hey.

130
00:16:28,841 --> 00:16:30,961
I ran into that kid in the forest.

131
00:16:32,131 --> 00:16:35,091
What? He's still alive?

132
00:16:35,181 --> 00:16:37,761
The blood of the Troll of Jom runs through his veins.

133
00:16:37,851 --> 00:16:39,971
He's not going to die that easily.

134
00:16:45,561 --> 00:16:47,651
Like father, like son.

135
00:17:16,431 --> 00:17:19,851
You can't let your sword
swing you around like that.

136
00:18:16,401 --> 00:18:17,401
Damn.

137
00:19:19,971 --> 00:19:22,011
We ended up staying here for a long time.

138
00:19:22,091 --> 00:19:24,511
I feel great now.

139
00:19:24,601 --> 00:19:26,561
What a comfortable village.

140
00:19:26,641 --> 00:19:27,641
Someone's coming.

141
00:19:36,231 --> 00:19:38,741
I'm Thors' son, Thorfinn.

142
00:19:39,611 --> 00:19:41,611
In the name of Odin, the Almighty,

143
00:19:42,821 --> 00:19:44,871
I challenge you to a duel.

144
00:19:46,781 --> 00:19:48,871
Come on. You're so annoying.

145
00:19:49,331 --> 00:19:51,661
You're pretty brave.

146
00:19:51,751 --> 00:19:53,751
Accept the duel, Askeladd.

147
00:19:56,711 --> 00:19:58,171
It's decided, then.

148
00:19:58,251 --> 00:20:01,221
It's the leader's job to meet his men's expectations.

149
00:20:07,971 --> 00:20:11,681
I, Askeladd, son of Olaf,
swear in the name of Odin

150
00:20:11,771 --> 00:20:14,851
that I accept your duel,
because I have no choice.

151
00:20:18,481 --> 00:20:19,781
Come on.

152
00:20:19,861 --> 00:20:22,361
Are you that eager to go meet your father?

153
00:21:01,441 --> 00:21:02,991
It's over.

154
00:21:03,071 --> 00:21:04,531
He can't win.

155
00:21:10,161 --> 00:21:11,331
Come on.

156
00:21:12,501 --> 00:21:14,411
Have you finished?

157
00:21:15,711 --> 00:21:17,831
How boring.

158
00:21:17,921 --> 00:21:19,461
Get up.

159
00:21:20,501 --> 00:21:21,841
This is a duel.

160
00:21:21,921 --> 00:21:25,341
I think that's enough. He's going to die.

161
00:21:27,301 --> 00:21:31,601
What's wrong?
You're the one who told me to kill him.

162
00:21:54,161 --> 00:21:57,581
That's it. I've had enough.

163
00:21:58,291 --> 00:22:00,751
I don't enjoy killing kids.

164
00:22:02,751 --> 00:22:04,211
Why?

165
00:22:04,301 --> 00:22:05,551
What do you mean?

166
00:22:05,631 --> 00:22:08,221
I'm busy too.

167
00:22:08,301 --> 00:22:09,431
Wait.

168
00:22:09,511 --> 00:22:11,391
I haven't lost.

169
00:22:11,471 --> 00:22:13,851
Fight. You coward.

170
00:22:14,311 --> 00:22:16,181
You're persistent, kid.

171
00:22:16,271 --> 00:22:17,941
It's not over yet.

172
00:22:18,021 --> 00:22:19,981
It's not over until I kill you.

173
00:22:20,061 --> 00:22:21,611
I swear, I will kill you.

174
00:22:27,701 --> 00:22:29,781
Try achieving something great on the battlefield.

175
00:22:31,031 --> 00:22:32,991
You're a Viking, right?

176
00:22:34,701 --> 00:22:35,751
Then...

177
00:22:36,791 --> 00:22:39,291
I'll reward you with a duel.

178
00:22:48,091 --> 00:22:49,301
That's a promise?

179
00:22:49,931 --> 00:22:53,051
Right. A promise between warriors.

180
00:22:58,891 --> 00:23:00,561
I'll achieve something in no time.

181
00:23:02,731 --> 00:23:04,231
And then...

182
00:23:05,531 --> 00:23:06,691
you'll die...

183
00:23:07,901 --> 00:23:09,201
by my hands.
